(* VimMotions — battallion's keymap: modes, motions, search and the editing keys.
 *
 * A plugin. It imports `Api` for the state operations and `Key` for the key values, holds no
 * authority, no pid and no descriptor, and its whole effect on the editor is the state it returns.
 * The kernel hands it the `api` record and a command interpreter and folds its `onKey` over the
 * decoded keys.
 *
 * ONE KEY IN, ONE STATE OUT. `onKey (api, commands, st, k)` returns `(state', quit)`; `quit` is
 * true when the key ends the session. A key that asks for something the kernel must do — a write —
 * leaves a request in the state instead (`api.requestWrite`), which the kernel carries out before
 * folding the keys behind it.
 *
 * THE COMMAND WORD IS NOT THIS PLUGIN'S. `:` opens the command line and this module edits it, but
 * what a command *means* is FileOps.trp's: on Enter the line is handed to the `commands` function
 * the kernel passed in, with the mode already back to normal and the line cleared. `q` and CTRL-c
 * go through the same function as the word "q", which is what makes them refuse a modified buffer
 * exactly as `:q` does.
 *
 * NORMAL MODE. `h j k l` and the arrows move by one; `0` and Home go to the line's start, `^` to
 * its first non-blank, `$` and End to its end; `w` and `b` move by a word; `gg` and `G` go to the
 * first and last line; PageUp/PageDown and CTRL-b/CTRL-f move by one screen. `i` enters insert
 * mode, `o` opens a line below and enters it, `x` deletes the character under the cursor, `dd`
 * deletes the line, `yy` yanks it, `p` and `P` put it back below and above, `u` undoes, `/` starts
 * a search and `n` and `N` repeat it, `:` starts a command line. `q` and CTRL-c quit, refusing on a
 * modified buffer exactly as `:q` does. CTRL-c quits because in raw mode it arrives as the byte
 * 0x03 with no signal raised, so without a binding the habit of pressing it would do nothing at
 * all. Every other key is ignored.
 *
 * INSERT MODE. A printable key inserts itself, whatever it is: the payload of `KEY_PRINT` is one
 * code point as a string and it goes into the buffer as it stands, so a multibyte character typed
 * or pasted is stored as typed. Enter splits the line, Tab inserts a tab, Backspace deletes the
 * character to the left and joins with the line above when there is none, Delete removes the
 * character under the cursor, Esc returns to normal mode. Motions work in insert mode too.
 *
 * COMMAND MODE IS ONE MODE FOR TWO PROMPTS. `:` opens it with a colon and `/` with a slash, and
 * `st.prompt` is which. The editing is the same either way — printable keys extend the line,
 * Backspace shortens it and leaves the mode when the line is empty, as backspacing over the colon
 * does in vi, Esc cancels — and only Enter looks at the prompt, handing a colon line to the
 * command interpreter and a slash line to the search below. One mode rather than two because the
 * status line has one row for both and because a second mode would be the same nine keys again.
 *
 * A TWO-KEY SEQUENCE IS A PREFIX IN THE STATE. `gg`, `dd` and `yy` are the pairs, and `st.pending`
 * holds the first key of one until the next key arrives. The rule is the whole mechanism: in
 * normal mode, a key that arrives with a prefix waiting is looked up as a *pair* and the prefix is
 * cleared, whether or not the pair is bound. So `d` then `x` does nothing and leaves normal mode
 * where it was, Esc after a prefix is a way to abandon it, and no key can be left half-pressed.
 * The prefix is shown at the end of the status line, so a `g` pressed by accident is visible
 * rather than silent. A prefix does not survive into insert or command mode, there being no pair
 * to complete it there, and it is not in an undo snapshot (Api.trp).
 *
 * SEARCH IS PLAIN TEXT, CASE-SENSITIVE, AND WRAPS. `/text` searches forward from just after the
 * cursor; `n` repeats it and `N` runs it backwards, both from wherever the cursor is now. The
 * pattern is a substring, not a regular expression: what is typed is what is looked for, and `.`
 * and `*` match themselves. Case is not folded — `/the` does not find `The` — because a search
 * that ignored case would need a way to say when it should not, and the editor has no options to
 * say it in. A search that reaches the end of the buffer continues from the top and says so in
 * the status line; one that finds nothing says that instead and leaves the cursor where it was. A
 * pattern is matched within one line: the buffer is scanned line by line, so a pattern cannot span
 * a line break — which nothing typed at the prompt can contain anyway.
 *
 * A WORD IS A RUN OF ONE CHARACTER CLASS. `w` and `b` divide the text into three classes — spaces
 * and tabs, word characters (letters, digits, underscore, and everything above ASCII), and
 * everything else — and move to the start of the next or the previous run that is not spaces,
 * crossing line breaks as vi does. An empty line is a word of its own and both keys stop on it.
 * Treating every character above ASCII as a word character is what keeps a word of accented
 * letters one word; it also makes a run of box-drawing characters one, which is the price.
 *
 * THE LINEWISE KEYS LAND AT COLUMN ZERO. `gg`, `G`, `dd` and `:N` put the cursor at the start of
 * the line rather than at its first non-blank, which is where vi puts it. `^` is the key that
 * finds the first non-blank, and it is one keystroke away from any of them.
 *
 * THE YANK REGISTER IS ONE LINE. `yy` takes the cursor's line, `dd` takes the line it deletes, and
 * `p` and `P` put whichever was taken last below or above the cursor's line. There is no charwise
 * yank and there are no named registers: a delete that is not linewise (`x`) does not touch the
 * register, so what `p` puts back is always a whole line.
 *
 * WHAT A VI USER WILL STILL MISS. There is no count prefix, so `5j` is five presses of `j`. Undo is
 * per keystroke, so a typed word takes as many `u`s as it had letters. `x` at the end of a line
 * does nothing where vi steps left onto the last character first, and leaving insert mode does not
 * pull the cursor left (Api.trp's header says where that choice lives).
 *)

import String
import List
import Option
import "./Api"
import "./Key"

let (*-----------------------------------  Messages  ----------------------------------*)

    val noPatternMessage     = "no previous search pattern"
    val wrapDownMessage      = "search hit the bottom, continuing at the top"
    val wrapUpMessage        = "search hit the top, continuing at the bottom"
    val nothingYankedMessage = "nothing has been yanked"
    val yankedMessage        = "line yanked"

    fun notFoundMessage p = "pattern not found: " ^ p

    (*-------------------------------  Character classes  -----------------------------*)

    (* The classes `w` and `b` move between: 0 is a space, 1 is a word character, 2 is anything
     * else. Everything above ASCII is class 1, so an accented word is one word. *)
    val classSpace = 0
    val classWord  = 1
    val classOther = 2

    fun classOf c =
        if c = " " orelse c = "\t" then classSpace
        else let val u = String.subCode (c, 0)
             in if (u >= 48 andalso u <= 57)
                   orelse (u >= 65 andalso u <= 90)
                   orelse (u >= 97 andalso u <= 122)
                   orelse u = 95
                   orelse u >= 128
                then classWord else classOther
             end

    fun classIn (line, i) = classOf (String.sub (line, i))

    (*---------------------------------  Word motions  --------------------------------*)

    (** The column on `line` where the next word begins, at or after `c`, or -1 when the line has
     *  no word start left in it: the run under the cursor is skipped, then the spaces after it. *)
    fun nextWordIn (line, n, c) =
        let fun skip (i, k) = if i < n andalso classIn (line, i) = k then skip (i + 1, k) else i
            val here  = if c < n then classIn (line, c) else classSpace
            val after = if here = classSpace then c else skip (c, here)
            val start = skip (after, classSpace)
        in if start < n then start else -1
        end

    (** The column on `line` where the word before `c` begins, or -1 when there is none: the spaces
     *  before `c` are stepped over, then the run they end. *)
    fun prevWordIn (line, n, c) =
        let val from = if c > n then n else c
            fun skipSpace i = if i >= 0 andalso classIn (line, i) = classSpace
                              then skipSpace (i - 1) else i
            val i = skipSpace (from - 1)
        in if i < 0 then -1
           else let val k = classIn (line, i)
                    fun back j = if j >= 0 andalso classIn (line, j) = k
                                 then back (j - 1) else j + 1
                in back i
                end
        end

    (** The cursor at the start of the next word, crossing line breaks; the end of the buffer stops
     *  it. `fresh` says the line was reached by crossing a break, in which case a word starting at
     *  its first column is the answer and an empty line is one too. *)
    fun wordForward (api, st) =
        let val last = api.lastLine st
            fun seek (l, c, fresh) =
                let val line = api.lineAt (st, l)
                    val n    = String.size line
                in if fresh andalso (n = 0 orelse classIn (line, 0) <> classSpace)
                   then api.moveTo (st, l, 0)
                   else let val hit = nextWordIn (line, n, c)
                        in if hit >= 0 then api.moveTo (st, l, hit)
                           else if l < last then seek (l + 1, 0, true)
                           else api.moveTo (st, l, n)
                        end
                end
        in seek (st.line, st.col, false)
        end

    (** The cursor at the start of the previous word, crossing line breaks; the start of the buffer
     *  stops it. An empty line reached by crossing a break is a word. *)
    fun wordBackward (api, st) =
        let fun seek (l, c, fresh) =
                let val line = api.lineAt (st, l)
                    val n    = String.size line
                in if fresh andalso n = 0
                   then api.moveTo (st, l, 0)
                   else let val hit = prevWordIn (line, n, c)
                        in if hit >= 0 then api.moveTo (st, l, hit)
                           else if l > 0 then seek (l - 1, Api.goalEnd, true)
                           else api.moveTo (st, l, 0)
                        end
                end
        in seek (st.line, st.col, false)
        end

    (** The column of the line's first character that is not a space, or its end when it has
     *  none. *)
    fun firstNonBlank (api, st, l) =
        let val line = api.lineAt (st, l)
            val n    = String.size line
            fun go i = if i < n andalso classIn (line, i) = classSpace then go (i + 1) else i
        in go 0
        end

    (*------------------------------------  Search  -----------------------------------*)

    (** The first hit at or after `(l0, c0)`, scanning to the last line: `SOME (line, col)` or
     *  `NONE`. One `strIndexOf` per line, so a miss costs a scan of the text below the cursor. *)
    fun hitFrom (api, st, pat, l0, c0) =
        let val last = api.lastLine st
            fun go (l, from) =
                if l > last then NONE
                else let val i = strIndexOf (api.lineAt (st, l), pat, from)
                     in if i >= 0 then SOME (l, i) else go (l + 1, 0)
                     end
        in go (l0, c0)
        end

    (** The last hit on `line` that begins before column `limit`, or -1. *)
    fun lastHitIn (line, pat, limit) =
        let fun go (i, best) =
                let val j = strIndexOf (line, pat, i)
                in if j < 0 orelse j >= limit then best else go (j + 1, j)
                end
        in go (0, -1)
        end

    (** The last hit before `(l0, c0)`, scanning upwards to the first line. *)
    fun hitBefore (api, st, pat, l0, c0) =
        let fun go (l, limit) =
                if l < 0 then NONE
                else let val i = lastHitIn (api.lineAt (st, l), pat, limit)
                     in if i >= 0 then SOME (l, i) else go (l - 1, Api.goalEnd)
                     end
        in go (l0, c0)
        end

    (** The state at the next hit of `pat`, or where it was with a message. `down` is the
     *  direction. A search that runs off the end continues from the other one, which is what makes
     *  `n` on the last hit come back to the first; the wrap is reported, a miss is reported, and a
     *  hit that needed neither says nothing. *)
    fun searchFor (api, st, pat, down) =
        let val (hit, wrapped) =
                if down
                then case hitFrom (api, st, pat, st.line, st.col + 1) of
                          SOME p => (SOME p, false)
                        | NONE   => (hitFrom (api, st, pat, 0, 0), true)
                else case hitBefore (api, st, pat, st.line, st.col) of
                          SOME p => (SOME p, false)
                        | NONE   => (hitBefore (api, st, pat, api.lastLine st, Api.goalEnd), true)
            val note = if down then wrapDownMessage else wrapUpMessage
        in case hit of
                NONE        => api.setStatus (st, notFoundMessage pat)
              | SOME (l, c) =>
                  let val st' = api.moveTo (st, l, c)
                  in if wrapped then api.setStatus (st', note) else st'
                  end
        end

    (** The pattern typed at the `/` prompt, remembered and run. An empty pattern repeats the last
     *  one, as vi's does. *)
    fun runSearch (api, st, pat) =
        if pat = ""
        then if st.find = "" then api.setStatus (st, noPatternMessage)
             else searchFor (api, st, st.find, true)
        else searchFor (api, api.setFind (st, pat), pat, true)

    (** `n` and `N`: the last pattern again, forward or backward. *)
    fun repeatSearch (api, st, down) =
        if st.find = "" then api.setStatus (st, noPatternMessage)
        else searchFor (api, st, st.find, down)

    (*------------------------------  Yanking and putting  ----------------------------*)

    fun yankLine (api, st) =
        api.setStatus (api.setYank (st, SOME (api.lineAt (st, st.line))), yankedMessage)

    fun putLine (api, st, below) =
        case st.yank of
             NONE   => api.setStatus (st, nothingYankedMessage)
           | SOME s => if below then api.putBelow (st, s) else api.putAbove (st, s)

    (*-----------------------------------  Motions  -----------------------------------*)

    (** The motions, shared by normal and insert mode. The vertical ones go through `moveLine`,
     *  which keeps the goal column, and the horizontal ones through `moveTo` and `moveEnd`, which
     *  set it (Api.trp). Any other key leaves the state alone. *)
    fun motion (api, st, KEY_LEFT)     = api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col - 1)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_RIGHT)    = api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col + 1)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_DOWN)     = api.moveLine (st, st.line + 1)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_UP)       = api.moveLine (st, st.line - 1)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_HOME)     = api.moveTo (st, st.line, 0)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_END)      = api.moveEnd (st, st.line)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_PAGEDOWN) = api.moveLine (st, st.line + api.textRows st)
      | motion (api, st, KEY_PAGEUP)   = api.moveLine (st, st.line - api.textRows st)
      | motion (api, st, _)            = st

    (*-------------------------------  Two-key sequences  -----------------------------*)

    (** The key that completes a prefix. The prefix is already cleared from `st`: a pair that is
     *  not bound leaves the state as it stands, so no key can be left half-pressed. *)
    fun pendingKey (api, st, prefix, KEY_PRINT c) =
             if prefix = "g" andalso c = "g" then (api.moveTo (st, 0, 0), false)
        else if prefix = "d" andalso c = "d" then (api.deleteLine (yankLine (api, st)), false)
        else if prefix = "y" andalso c = "y" then (yankLine (api, st), false)
        else (st, false)
      | pendingKey (api, st, prefix, k) = (st, false)

    (*--------------------------------  Normal mode  ---------------------------------*)

    fun normalPrint (api, commands, st, c) =
             if c = "h" then (api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col - 1), false)
        else if c = "l" then (api.moveTo (st, st.line, st.col + 1), false)
        else if c = "j" then (api.moveLine (st, st.line + 1), false)
        else if c = "k" then (api.moveLine (st, st.line - 1), false)
        else if c = "0" then (api.moveTo (st, st.line, 0), false)
        else if c = "^" then (api.moveTo (st, st.line, firstNonBlank (api, st, st.line)), false)
        else if c = "$" then (api.moveEnd (st, st.line), false)
        else if c = "w" then (wordForward (api, st), false)
        else if c = "b" then (wordBackward (api, st), false)
        else if c = "G" then (api.moveTo (st, api.lastLine st, 0), false)
        else if c = "i" then (api.setMode (st, INSERT), false)
        else if c = "o" then (api.openBelow st, false)
        else if c = "x" then (api.deleteChar st, false)
        else if c = "p" then (putLine (api, st, true), false)
        else if c = "P" then (putLine (api, st, false), false)
        else if c = "u" then (api.undo st, false)
        else if c = "n" then (repeatSearch (api, st, true), false)
        else if c = "N" then (repeatSearch (api, st, false), false)
        else if c = "/" then (api.openPrompt (st, "/"), false)
        else if c = ":" then (api.openPrompt (st, ":"), false)
        else if c = "g" orelse c = "d" orelse c = "y" then (api.setPending (st, c), false)
        else if c = "q" then commands (st, "q")
        else (st, false)

    fun normalKey (api, commands, st, KEY_PRINT c) = normalPrint (api, commands, st, c)
      | normalKey (api, commands, st, KEY_CTRL c) =
             if c = "f" then (api.moveLine (st, st.line + api.textRows st), false)
        else if c = "b" then (api.moveLine (st, st.line - api.textRows st), false)
        else if c = "c" then commands (st, "q")
        else (st, false)
      | normalKey (api, commands, st, KEY_DELETE) = (api.deleteChar st, false)
      | normalKey (api, commands, st, k)          = (motion (api, st, k), false)

    (*--------------------------------  Insert mode  ---------------------------------*)

    fun insertKey (api, st, KEY_PRINT c)   = (api.insertText (st, c), false)
      | insertKey (api, st, KEY_ENTER)     = (api.insertText (st, "\n"), false)
      | insertKey (api, st, KEY_TAB)       = (api.insertText (st, "\t"), false)
      | insertKey (api, st, KEY_BACKSPACE) = (api.backspace st, false)
      | insertKey (api, st, KEY_DELETE)    = (api.deleteChar st, false)
      | insertKey (api, st, KEY_ESC)       = (api.setMode (st, NORMAL), false)
      | insertKey (api, st, k)             = (motion (api, st, k), false)

    (*--------------------------------  Command mode  --------------------------------*)

    (** What Enter does with the line is what the prompt says: a command word goes to the command
     *  interpreter, a search pattern to the search above. *)
    fun runPrompt (api, commands, st, prompt, line) =
        if prompt = "/" then (runSearch (api, st, line), false) else commands (st, line)

    fun commandKey (api, commands, st, KEY_PRINT c) = (api.setCmd (st, st.cmd ^ c), false)
      | commandKey (api, commands, st, KEY_ENTER)   =
          runPrompt (api, commands, api.closePrompt st, st.prompt, st.cmd)
      | commandKey (api, commands, st, KEY_ESC)     = (api.closePrompt st, false)
      | commandKey (api, commands, st, KEY_BACKSPACE) =
          if st.cmd = "" then (api.closePrompt st, false)
          else (api.setCmd (st, String.substring (st.cmd, 0, String.size st.cmd - 1)), false)
      | commandKey (api, commands, st, KEY_CTRL c) =
          if c = "c" then (api.closePrompt st, false) else (st, false)
      | commandKey (api, commands, st, _) = (st, false)

    (*----------------------------------  Help mode  ---------------------------------*)

    (** Any key at all puts the help page away and the buffer back. Nothing else in the state is
     *  touched, so the key that dismissed the page is spent on dismissing it. *)
    fun helpKey (api, st, k) = (api.setMode (st, NORMAL), false)

    (*-----------------------------------  The map  ----------------------------------*)

    (** `(state', quit)` for one key.
     *
     *  A transient status message is cleared here rather than where it is set, so every message
     *  is shown for exactly as long as it takes the user to press the next key.
     *
     *  A prefix waiting in the state is spent here too, and only in normal mode: the key is looked
     *  up as a pair and the prefix is cleared whether or not the pair is bound. *)
    fun onKey (api, commands, st0, k) =
        let val st = if st0.status = "" then st0 else api.setStatus (st0, "")
        in case st.mode of
                INSERT  => insertKey (api, st, k)
              | COMMAND => commandKey (api, commands, st, k)
              | HELP    => helpKey (api, st, k)
              | _       => if st.pending = ""
                           then normalKey (api, commands, st, k)
                           else pendingKey (api, api.setPending (st, ""), st.pending, k)
        end

    (*----------------------------------  The help  ----------------------------------*)

    (** What `:help` says about this keymap: the sections the plugin set assembles the help page
     *  from (Help.trp). A key added above belongs in the section it belongs to here. *)
    val help =
        [ ("MOTION",
           [ ("h j k l",   "move by one")
           , ("arrows",    "move by one")
           , ("0 Home",    "start of the line")
           , ("^",         "first non-blank")
           , ("$ End",     "end of the line")
           , ("w b",       "next, previous word")
           , ("gg G",      "first, last line")
           , ("^B ^F",     "up, down a screen")
           , ("PgUp PgDn", "up, down a screen") ])
        , ("EDIT",
           [ ("i",         "insert before the cursor")
           , ("o",         "open a line below")
           , ("x Del",     "delete a character")
           , ("dd",        "delete the line")
           , ("yy",        "yank the line")
           , ("p P",       "put it below, above")
           , ("u",         "undo one change")
           , ("Esc",       "leave insert mode") ])
        , ("SEARCH",
           [ ("/text",     "search forward")
           , ("n N",       "next, previous match") ])
        , ("SESSION",
           [ (":",         "start a command")
           , ("q ^C",      "quit like :q") ])
        ]

in [ ("onKey", onKey)
   , ("help", help)
   ]
end
